import ../../../ui/shaders.dl

class:
    patterns:
        shader API recorder
    members:
        frames as an integer
        vertices as an integer
        indices as an integer
        draws as an integer
        closed as an integer

to get [the shader recorder in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    return view's instance's state as a pointer to shader API recorder

to get [render recorded shader in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [holding] {a pointer:shader} [sized] {integer:width} [by] {integer:height} [using] {C string:data} [counting] {integer:count}:
    require condition ((shader = (777 as a pointer)) and ((width = 40) and (height = 20))) reporting "Shader frame arguments changed across the driver boundary."
    require condition ((count = 4) and ((the character at 0 in data) = 91)) reporting "Shader values were not transferred as source bytes."
    increment (the shader recorder in view)'s frames
    return 910 as a pointer

to [upload recorded shader in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [holding] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [slot] {integer:slot} [from] {a pointer:data} [counting] {integer:count}:
    require condition ((shader = (777 as a pointer)) and ((pass = 2) and (slot = 3))) reporting "Vertex upload lost its shader/pass/slot."
    require condition ((count = 8) and ((the item at 1 in (data as a pointer to a 32 bit floating-point number)) = 2.0)) reporting "Vertex uploads assumed a fixed four-float record."
    increment (the shader recorder in view)'s vertices

to [index recorded shader in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [holding] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [from] {a pointer to a 32 bit unsigned integer:data} [counting] {integer:count}:
    require condition ((pass = 2) and ((count = 3) and ((the item at 2 in data) = 2))) reporting "Index upload changed its count or data."
    increment (the shader recorder in view)'s indices

to [draw recorded shader in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [holding] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [from] {a pointer to UI shader draw:data} [counting] {integer:count}:
    require condition ((pass = 2) and (count = 2)) reporting "Draw submission changed its record count."
    set first to the item at 0 in data
    set last to the item at 1 in data
    require condition (((first's count = 3) and (first's vertex offset = 4)) and (first's indexed = 1)) reporting "Indexed draw data did not cross the driver intact."
    require condition (((last's instances = 2) and (last's instance offset = 7)) and (last's indexed = 0)) reporting "Instanced draw data did not cross the driver intact."
    increment (the shader recorder in view)'s draws

to get [recorded shader bytes in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [holding] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [slot] {integer:slot}:
    return 48

to get [recorded shader records in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [holding] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [slot] {integer:slot}:
    return 3

to get [recorded shader indices in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [holding] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass}:
    return 6

to [close recorded shader in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [holding] {a pointer:shader}:
    increment (the shader recorder in view)'s closed

set operations to @intrinsic("construct", UI shader operations,
    (the function named "render recorded shader in $ holding $ sized $ by $ using $ counting $") as a pointer,
    (the function named "upload recorded shader in $ holding $ pass $ slot $ from $ counting $") as a pointer,
    (the function named "index recorded shader in $ holding $ pass $ from $ counting $") as a pointer,
    (the function named "draw recorded shader in $ holding $ pass $ from $ counting $") as a pointer,
    (the function named "recorded shader bytes in $ holding $ pass $ slot $") as a pointer,
    (the function named "recorded shader records in $ holding $ pass $ slot $") as a pointer,
    (the function named "recorded shader indices in $ holding $ pass $") as a pointer,
    (the function named "close recorded shader in $ holding $") as a pointer)
set driver to a new UI driver
set driver's shader operations to the address of operations
set recorder to a new shader API recorder
set instance to a new UI instance
set instance's state to (the address of recorder) as a pointer
set view to a new UI view
set view's instance to the address of instance
set view's driver to the address of driver
set context to the address of view
set shader to 777 as a pointer
require condition ((the size of UI shader draw) = 24) reporting "Draw records do not have a portable six-word layout."
require condition ((4294967299 is a valid UI operation integer) = false) reporting "An oversized range was narrowed before validation."
set maximum to a UI shader draw counting 2147483647 instanced 2147483647 starting at 2147483647 with vertex offset 2147483647 and instance offset 2147483647 indexed false
require condition ((maximum's count = 2147483647) and (maximum's instance offset = 2147483647)) reporting "A valid maximum range was narrowed."
set vertices to [1.0,2.0] as a 32 bit floating-point number array of 2 items
set indices to [0,1,2] as a 32 bit unsigned integer array of 3 items
set draws to [
    a UI shader draw counting 3 instanced 1 starting at 0 with vertex offset 4 and instance offset 0 indexed true,
    a UI shader draw counting 3 instanced 2 starting at 1 with vertex offset 0 and instance offset 7 indexed false
]
set UI shader shader pass 2 in context vertex buffer 3 from ((vertices + 0) as a pointer) spanning 8 bytes
set UI shader shader pass 2 in context to indices (indices + 0) counting 3
set UI shader shader pass 2 in context to draws (draws + 0) counting 2
require condition ((the byte count of UI shader shader pass 2 buffer 3 in context) = 48) reporting "Shader buffer size queries did not use the driver."
require condition ((the record count of UI shader shader pass 2 buffer 3 in context) = 3) reporting "Shader buffer record queries did not use the driver."
require condition ((the index count of UI shader shader pass 2 in context) = 6) reporting "Shader index count queries did not use the driver."
set image to a UI texture from shader shader sized 40 by 20 using (the string form of "[{}]") in context
require condition ((image's resource = (910 as a pointer)) and ((image's width = 40) and (image's height = 20))) reporting "Shader texture data changed across drivers."
set encoded to the JSON form of UI shader draw (the item at 0 in draws)
require condition (((the JSON number named "vertexOffset" in encoded) = 4.0) and (the JSON boolean named "indexed" in encoded)) reporting "Draw descriptors and binary submissions disagree."
free encoded
close UI shader shader in context
require condition (((recorder's frames = 1) and (recorder's vertices = 1)) and (((recorder's indices = 1) and (recorder's draws = 1)) and (recorder's closed = 1))) reporting "Shader driver callbacks were omitted or repeated."
print line "Shared shader operations transfer raw buffers, draw records and texture ownership through a platform driver."
